        "title": "normalizeGitHubActor: not idempotent — strips only one trailing [bot]",
        "body": "`normalizeGitHubActor(login)` in `src/repair/comment-router-utils.ts:185` strips a single trailing `[bot]` via `/\\[bot\\]$/i`, so a doubled suffix leaves a residual that a second pass strips again.\n\nRepro:\n```\nnormalizeGitHubActor(\"x[bot][bot]\") === \"x[bot]\"\nnormalizeGitHubActor(\"x[bot]\")      === \"x\"        // => not idempotent\n```\nA normalizer should be idempotent. Loop/global-strip the suffix (though a doubled [bot] is rare in practice). Related: `stripEnvPrefix` in `repair/validation-command-utils.ts` has the same single-pass shape.",
